  "title": "About me",
  "goal": "Introduce yourself: say your name, where you are from, where you live and which languages you speak, and ask others the same.",
  "intro": "In this unit you meet the Telugu pronouns and learn how to say 'I am...'. Telugu needs **no verb at all** to say who someone is (*నేను సారా*, I [am] Sara), but uses the verb *ఉండు* (uṇḍu) to say where someone is.\n\nYou'll also meet the core question words. Notice how Telugu asks 'where are you from?': *మీది ఏ ఊరు?* (mīdi ē ūru?), literally 'yours is which town?'",
